WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:15.852
"Trolls!" Zann shouted. "Run!"

2
00:00:15.853 --> 00:00:20.090
"Run where?" Perda exclaimed. "We're surrounded!"

3
00:00:20.091 --> 00:00:23.480
Zann rubbed his hands together, preparing to zap away.

4
00:00:23.481 --> 00:00:26.255
But one of the trolls was looming over Darb.

5
00:00:26.256 --> 00:00:29.436
There was no way Zann could grab his friend and escape.

6
00:00:29.437 --> 00:00:35.364
Besides, the biggest troll had just grabbed Gliss by the arm. They were trapped!

7
00:00:35.365 --> 00:00:38.670
Suddenly a sheet of flame surrounded the big troll.

8
00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:45.784
The troll grunted, a dull look of surprise crossing its singed face. Gliss shrieked and pulled free.

9
00:00:45.785 --> 00:00:47.912
"Zing!" Darb cried.

10
00:00:47.913 --> 00:00:52.591
The dragon spat out another burst of flame at the second troll, who tried to grab him.

11
00:00:52.592 --> 00:00:57.478
But Zing flew up and circled overhead, whistling the song his breed was named for.

12
00:00:57.479 --> 00:01:00.225
It sounded like an ordinary tune to people.

13
00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:04.416
But for most other creatures, the song had a hypnotizing effect.

14
00:01:04.417 --> 00:01:07.495
The trolls turned in circles, staring up at Zing.

15
00:01:07.496 --> 00:01:11.128
"Zing's song is distracting them!" Zann cried.

16
00:01:11.129 --> 00:01:15.814
The trolls didn't look fully hypnotized, though; they just looked confused.

17
00:01:15.815 --> 00:01:18.746
Zann knew they would probably recover in a second.

18
00:01:18.747 --> 00:01:23.047
"Go!" he urged, giving Darb a shove to get him started.

19
00:01:23.048 --> 00:01:27.003
The kids pushed past the confused trolls and sprinted toward the swamp.

20
00:01:27.004 --> 00:01:30.898
"Do you think Morb sent those trolls?" Gliss called out.

21
00:01:30.899 --> 00:01:33.767
Zann glanced back at her. "He must have.

22
00:01:33.768 --> 00:01:38.659
I guess that proves he's tracking all of our magic, not just mine."

23
00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:42.163
"Faster!" Perda panted as she passed Zann.

24
00:01:42.164 --> 00:01:47.843
"We have to get out of sight before Morb shows up to see what's taking the trolls so long."

25
00:01:47.844 --> 00:01:52.567
Darb jumped into the lead. "Come this way. I know a shortcut back to the Hollow."

26
00:01:52.568 --> 00:01:55.272
They all changed directions to follow him.

27
00:01:55.273 --> 00:01:59.979
As a Void, Darb had to rely on his own two feet to get places most of the time.

28
00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:02.734
He was sure to know the shortest route.

29
00:02:02.735 --> 00:02:07.718
They had almost reached the Hollow when Zann felt something splash onto his head.

30
00:02:07.719 --> 00:02:11.440
"Uh-oh," he said. "It's starting to rain."

31
00:02:11.441 --> 00:02:15.136
Perda made a face as a drop of orange water hit her arm.

32
00:02:15.137 --> 00:02:19.781
"Ugh. It's an orange rain this time," she complained.

33
00:02:19.782 --> 00:02:24.297
Zann's fingers twitched, but he stopped himself from conjuring up an umbrella.

34
00:02:24.298 --> 00:02:27.289
Orange was his least favorite type of rain.

35
00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:31.225
It stained clothes and skin worse than any other color.

36
00:02:31.226 --> 00:02:33.741
By now they were in sight of the Hollow.

37
00:02:33.742 --> 00:02:37.732
They heard a triumphant whistle, and Zing came speeding past.

38
00:02:37.733 --> 00:02:42.483
He did a flip in the air and landed in front of Darb.

39
00:02:42.484 --> 00:02:49.503
"Good job, little buddy," Zann told the dragon, scratching him under his scaly snout. "You saved us."

40
00:02:49.504 --> 00:02:53.606
They all ducked into the Hollow as the rain started coming down harder.

41
00:02:53.607 --> 00:02:57.835
But there was nothing to cover them, and they were all soon soaked to the skin.

42
00:02:57.836 --> 00:03:03.535
"I wish we could conjure up some shelter," Gliss complained as they huddled together for warmth.

43
00:03:03.536 --> 00:03:06.336
"Me too." Zann sighed.

44
00:03:06.337 --> 00:03:09.072
An hour later the rain finally stopped.

45
00:03:09.073 --> 00:03:12.568
The entire swamp had a bright orange sheen.

46
00:03:12.569 --> 00:03:15.693
"Let's go find that diary," Zann said.

47
00:03:15.694 --> 00:03:18.823
"Maybe we should split up," Perda suggested.

48
00:03:18.824 --> 00:03:24.425
"Two of us could look for the diary while the other two go tell the mayor what we know about Morb.

49
00:03:24.426 --> 00:03:27.619
She might be able to help us contact the palace."

50
00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:32.452
"No!" Gliss exclaimed. "Please, can't we stay together?"

51
00:03:32.453 --> 00:03:37.437
"She's right," Darb said. "It's definitely safer if we all stick together."

52
00:03:37.438 --> 00:03:43.190
Zann nodded. "We'll find the diary, and then we can all go see the mayor together."

53
00:03:43.191 --> 00:03:46.238
This time they let Zing come to town with them.

54
00:03:46.239 --> 00:03:50.981
The dragon whistled suspiciously when they passed the spot where the trolls had ambushed them.

55
00:03:50.982 --> 00:03:53.907
But there was no sign of the huge creatures now.

56
00:03:53.908 --> 00:03:58.682
When they reached Zann's house—or what was left of it—Zann gulped.

57
00:03:58.683 --> 00:04:05.531
Two walls were still half-intact, along with a few overhead beams, but the rest of the place was mostly rubble.

58
00:04:05.532 --> 00:04:12.621
The orange rain was already drying and fading, but a few rusty puddles remained, making things look even worse.

59
00:04:12.622 --> 00:04:19.134
"Oh, Zann!" Gliss cried. "This is horrible! You must be so upset!"

60
00:04:19.135 --> 00:04:24.079
"It's just a house," Zann said quickly. "Boz can fix it when he gets back."

61
00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:26.968
He stepped forward. "Let's start searching.

62
00:04:26.969 --> 00:04:32.745
The diary is small and has a bronze cover that looks like dragon scales."

63
00:04:32.746 --> 00:04:36.894
They climbed onto what used to be the inside of the house.

64
00:04:36.895 --> 00:04:39.814
Most of the furniture was smashed to bits.

65
00:04:39.815 --> 00:04:45.652
Zann paused and looked at his favorite lamp, which was broken in half. Then he kept going.

66
00:04:45.653 --> 00:04:50.655
He climbed over some fallen chunks of the walls, aiming for where the main room had been.

67
00:04:50.656 --> 00:04:53.620
Then he started digging through the rubble.

68
00:04:53.621 --> 00:04:59.319
When he moved a chunk of the ceiling out of the way, he saw that the table was mostly undamaged.

69
00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:02.600
"Aha!" Zann murmured as he peered under it.

70
00:05:02.601 --> 00:05:05.400
There was a book lying there—the diary!

71
00:05:05.401 --> 00:05:09.689
As he reached for the diary, he heard a sudden crunch of breaking wood.

72
00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:15.196
He jumped to his feet and realized that Perda and Gliss were standing near the side wall.

73
00:05:15.197 --> 00:05:20.669
One of them had just shoved aside a broken bookshelf, which had been holding up a large wooden beam.

74
00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:26.977
The girls were peering at something on the floor, completely unaware that the heavy beam was toppling right toward them!

75
00:05:26.978 --> 00:05:32.793
Zann gasped. Without thinking, he rubbed his fingers and pointed at the falling beam.

76
00:05:32.794 --> 00:05:37.254
The beam stopped short and floated in midair just above the girls' heads.

77
00:05:37.255 --> 00:05:40.794
Gliss and Perda glanced up, and then dashed away from it.

78
00:05:40.795 --> 00:05:43.628
"That was close!" Gliss exclaimed.

79
00:05:43.629 --> 00:05:55.665
Before Zann could answer, there was a blinding flash, and Morb appeared before them in a swirl of smoke!
